From 0f41264f73f985d5fb35b5c2a9e1daf021beab4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 21:37:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-30: mark the wiring state on the design surface --
 green / orange / red frames (0.30.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

右鍵 > 在畫面上標出接線狀態 (and the command palette): every component with
DFM events gets a coloured frame on the design surface -- green: the web
handles all of its events (a listener, or the wire engine's field map),
orange: some / only mentioned (delegated), red: none. A legend in the
corner, "接線標示" in the status bar; again = off. Kept across a re-draw (the
probe gets it with init). The data is the wiring overview's
(computeOverview, now shared by the overview tab and this); porting BCB6
pages, the buttons still to wire stand out at a glance.

Tests: probe (a red frame exactly on the button; off: gone), smoke 97
(sbtExit green with a click listener, spbSave orange -- delegated; status
bar), real VS Code 98 (the real listeners: HotPlate 9 green, 1 orange, 0
red; off again), lib 121, panels -- all pass; NO-SAVES.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
